## Message Acknowledgement

The consumer uses **manual acknowledgements** (`noAck: false`). Never auto-ack.

| Outcome | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Email sent successfully | `channel.ack(msg)` |
| Transient failure (SMTP timeout) | Re-publish with incremented `x-retry-count` + backoff TTL; `channel.ack(msg)` original |
| Permanent failure (max retries exhausted) | `channel.nack(msg, false, false)` → DLQ |
| Invalid / malformed message | `channel.nack(msg, false, false)` → DLQ immediately |

---

## Idempotency Pattern

Before any processing, check whether `eventId` already exists in `notification_log`. If it does, ack and skip.

```js
const existing = await notificationRepository.findLogByEventId(eventId);
if (existing) {
    logger.warn({ eventId }, 'Duplicate event received — skipping');
    channel.ack(msg);
    return;
}
```

